<%
  var b = company.business;
  var d = shippingCfg.DISPATCH;
%>

<nav class="col-page__breadcrumb container" style="padding-top:1rem" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="<%= marketPath('/') %>">Home</a>
  <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <span aria-current="page">Shipping &amp; Delivery</span>
</nav>

<div class="container legal-page" style="padding-top:2rem;padding-bottom:4rem;max-width:56rem">
  <h1 class="heading-section">Shipping &amp; Delivery</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">
    Everything on this page is what the checkout actually does and what we
    declare to Google. There is one shipping policy and this is it.
  </p>

  <div class="ship-banner">
    <p class="ship-banner__head"><%= shippingCfg.copy.short %></p>
    <p class="ship-banner__sub">
      Every order ships tracked, at our cost, wherever you are. No minimum spend,
      no threshold to reach, and no cheaper untracked option to decline.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>How long it takes</h2>

  <%/* Rendered from config/shipping.js rather than written out by hand.
       The old version of this table lived in a database page as literal
       HTML while the Offer schema quoted a single flat US rate to every
       shopper on earth and the announcement bar quoted a third figure —
       three different answers to "what will delivery cost me", which is
       the "shipping mismatch" a Merchant Center reviewer catches by
       comparing the feed against this page. Now there is one source. */%>
  <div class="legal-table-wrap">
    <table class="legal-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">Carriers, delivery estimates and cost by destination. Shipping is free to every destination listed.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Destination</th>
          <th scope="col">Carrier</th>
          <th scope="col">Estimated delivery</th>
          <th scope="col">Cost</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% shippingCfg.REGIONS.forEach(function (r) { %>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><%= r.name %></th>
            <td><%= r.carrier %></td>
            <td><%= r.transitDays[0] %>&ndash;<%= r.transitDays[1] %> business days</td>
            <td class="ship-free">Free</td>
          </tr>
        <% }); %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Delivery estimates are counted from dispatch, not from when you order, and they
    are the carrier's estimate rather than a guarantee. All prices are in
    <%= b.currency %>.
  </p>

  <h2>When your order leaves us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      In-stock orders placed before <%= d.cutoffLocal %> <%= d.cutoffTimezone %> on a business day
      are dispatched the same day. After that, or at a weekend or public holiday,
      they go the next business day.
    </li>
    <li>
      Preorders ship on the publisher's release date, or within
      <%= d.preorderBusinessDaysAfterRelease %> business days of it. You are charged when you
      place the preorder, not on release day. See the full
      <a href="<%= marketPath('/collection/preorders') %>">preorder terms</a> on any preorder listing.
    </li>
    <li>
      You get a tracking number by email the moment the label is created.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tracking and cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every order ships tracked, with no exceptions and no cheaper untracked option.</li>
    <li>Every order is covered against loss or damage in transit. If it arrives damaged or does not arrive, that is our problem to fix, not yours to absorb.</li>
    <li>Orders over $<%= shippingCfg.SIGNATURE_REQUIRED_OVER_USD %> require a signature on delivery.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we pack</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Booster boxes and elite trainer boxes are individually wrapped before they go in the outer carton.</li>
    <li>Everything ships in a rigid corrugated box sized so the contents cannot move. Corners and seals are what a collector inspects first, so they are what the packaging is designed to protect.</li>
    <li>Master cases ship in the distributor's own sealed shipper, unopened.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>International orders, duties and taxes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Import duty, VAT and customs handling fees are set by the destination country,
      are charged to you by the carrier or the customs authority, and are
      <strong>not</strong> included in the price you pay us.
    </li>
    <li>
      We declare the true value of every shipment. We do not mark orders as gifts and
      we do not undervalue them. Being asked to is the one request we always refuse:
      it is customs fraud, and it is the buyer who carries the consequence.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a parcel is refused or abandoned at customs, the outbound and return carriage
      come out of the refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Returns</h2>
  <p>
    Unopened, still-sealed product can be returned within <%= returnWindowDays %> days of
    delivery. If an item arrives damaged or is not what you ordered we pay the return
    postage and you choose between a replacement and a full refund<% if (freeReturns) { %>;
    if you simply changed your mind, we pay the return postage on that too<% } else { %>; for a change of
    mind the return postage is yours<% } %>. The full terms, including how to start a return,
    are on the <a href="<%= marketPath('/refund-policy') %>">Refund Policy</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions about a shipment</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:<%= b.supportEmail %>"><%= b.supportEmail %></a> with your order
    number, or use the <a href="<%= marketPath('/contact') %>">contact form</a>. We reply within
    <%= b.responseTimeHours %> hours, <%= b.supportHours ? b.supportHours.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + b.supportHours.slice(1) : 'on business days' %>.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .legal-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 1.25rem 0 1rem; }
  .legal-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.86rem; min-width: 34rem; }
  .legal-table th, .legal-table td { text-align: left; padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); }
  .legal-table thead th { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--color-text-faint); }
  .legal-table tbody th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text); }
  .legal-table td { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .ship-free { color: var(--color-accent, #10B981) !important; font-weight: 700; }
  .ship-banner { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(124,58,237,0.12), rgba(6,182,212,0.08)); border: 1px solid rgba(124,58,237,0.3); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem; }
  .ship-banner__head { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-white); }
  .ship-banner__sub { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.75; margin-top: 0.4rem; max-width: 60ch; }
</style>
